# Nothing built ever goes in. The DLLs are produced from these sources with CMake; see README.md.
# The wildcard covers a second configure alongside the first, build-audit or build-x86 or
# whatever it gets called; those are as untrackable as build/ itself and easy to commit by
# accident, because git shows them and the reviewer sees one more directory rather than
# thirty megabytes.
build*/
*.obj
*.pdb
*.exp
*.lib
*.ilk
*.dll
*.exe

# Written next to the game, not here, but people do copy them back for a bug report.
engine_fixes.log
engine_fixes.prev.log
engine_fixes_diag.log

# A tuned copy someone dropped in the checkout. The one that ships is dist/engine_fixes.ini
# and is tracked; this only matches the repository root.
/engine_fixes.ini

# Working notes for splitting a branch into commits. Useful while the work is in progress and
# meaningless afterwards, so it stays out of the history rather than being deleted by hand.
/COMMIT-MESSAGES.txt
